  'second-largest-element-in-array', 'problem', 'Second largest element in array', '', 'published', 'public',
  'leetcode', '', 'medium', 'Arrays', 'Easy',
  '[]', '{"format":"sections","sections":[{"id":"statement","title":"Problem Statement","kind":"problem-statement","bodyMd":"Given an array Arr of size N, print second largest distinct element from an array.\n\nExample:\n\nInput:\nN = 6\nArr[] = {12, 35, 1, 10, 34, 1}\nOutput: 34\nExplanation: The largest element of the\narray is 35 and the second largest element\nis 34.","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-approach","title":"Brute Force Approach","kind":"solution","bodyMd":"","codeBlocks":[{"language":"java","title":"Brute Force Java","code":"int print2largest(int arr[], int n)\n{\n    int prev = -1, curr = arr[0];\n    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++)\n    {\n        if (arr[i] > curr)\n        {\n            prev = curr;\n            curr = arr[i];\n        }\n        else if (arr[i] > prev && arr[i] != curr)\n            prev = arr[i];\n    }\n    return prev;\n}"}],"metadata":{"time":"O(N)","space":"O(0)"},"visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-complexity","title":"Brute Force Complexity","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Time complexity: O(N)\nSpace complexity: O(0)","visuals":[]}]}', 
