) VALUES (
  'union-of-2-sorted-arrays', 'problem', 'Union of 2 sorted arrays', '', 'published', 'public',
  'leetcode', '', 'medium', 'Arrays', 'Easy',
  '[]', '{"format":"sections","sections":[{"id":"statement","title":"Problem Statement","kind":"problem-statement","bodyMd":"Union of two arrays can be defined as the common and distinct elements in the two arrays.\nGiven two sorted arrays of size n and m respectively, find their union.\n\n\nExample 1:\n\nInput:\nn = 5, arr1[] = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}\nm = 3, arr2 [] = {1, 2, 3}\nOutput: 1 2 3 4 5\nExplanation: Distinct elements including\nboth the arrays are: 1 2 3 4 5.\n\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput:\nn = 5, arr1[] = {2, 2, 3, 4, 5}\nm = 5, arr2[] = {1, 1, 2, 3, 4}\nOutput: 1 2 3 4 5\nExplanation: Distinct elements including\nboth the arrays are: 1 2 3 4 5.","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-intuition","title":"Brute Force Intuition","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Understand the problem and develop a solution approach.\n\n-> Take two pointer i and j where i is for arr1 and j is for arr2 and traverse\n-> While travsersing 3 cases arises\n    -> arr1[ i ] == arr2[ j ]\n        Here we found a common element, so insert only one element in the union.\n        Let’s insert arr[i] in union and whenever we insert element we increment pointer while pointer is not equal to the inserted element\n    -> arr1[i]<arr2[j]\n        Here insert arr[i]\n    -> arr1[i]>arr2[j]\n        Here insert arr2[j]\n-> Now check if elements of any array is left to traverse then traverse that array","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-approach","title":"Brute Force Approach","kind":"solution","bodyMd":"-> Take two pointer i and j where i is for arr1 and j is for arr2 and traverse\n-> While travsersing 3 cases arises\n    -> arr1[ i ] == arr2[ j ]\n        Here we found a common element, so insert only one element in the union.\n        Let’s insert arr[i] in union and whenever we insert element we increment pointer while pointer is not equal to the inserted element\n    -> arr1[i]<arr2[j]\n        Here insert arr[i]\n    -> arr1[i]>arr2[j]\n        Here insert arr2[j]\n-> Now check if elements of any array is left to traverse then traverse that array","codeBlocks":[{"language":"java","title":"Brute Force Java","code":"ArrayList<int> findUnion(int arr1[], int arr2[], int n, int m)\n{\n    int i = 0; // i to keep track in arr1\n    int j = 0; // j to keep track in arr2\n    ArrayList<int> ans;\n    while (i < n && j < m)\n    {\n\n        if (arr1[i] < arr2[j])\n        {\n            ans.add(arr1[i++]);\n            while (i < n && arr1[i] == arr1[i - 1])\n                i++;\n        }\n        else if (arr2[j] < arr1[i])\n        {\n            ans.add(arr2[j++]);\n            while (j < m && arr2[j] == arr2[j - 1])\n                j++;\n        }\n        // means arr1[i] = arr2[j] in that case we can insert anyone\n        else\n        {\n            ans.add(arr1[i++]);\n            j++;\n            while (i < n && arr1[i] == arr1[i - 1])\n                i++;\n            while (j < m && arr2[j] == arr2[j - 1])\n                j++;\n        }\n    }\n\n    while (i < n)\n    {\n        ans.add(arr1[i++]);\n        while (i < n && arr1[i] == arr1[i - 1])\n            i++;\n    }\n    while (j < m)\n    {\n        ans.add(arr2[j++]);\n        while (j < m && arr2[j] == arr2[j - 1])\n            j++;\n    }\n\n    return ans;\n}"}],"metadata":{"time":"O(N+M)","space":"O(0)"},"visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-complexity","title":"Brute Force Complexity","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Time complexity: O(N+M)\nSpace complexity: O(0)","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-quick-revision","title":"Brute Force Quick Revision","kind":"checklist","bodyMd":"- [ ] Take two pointer i and j where i is for arr1 and j is for arr2 and traverse\n- [ ] While travsersing 3 cases arises\n- [ ] -> arr1[ i ] == arr2[ j ]\n- [ ] Here we found a common element, so insert only one element in the union.\n- [ ] Let’s insert arr[i] in union and whenever we insert element we increment pointer while pointer is not equal to the inserted element"}]}', 
  '[]', '[]', '[]',
  'union-of-2-sorted-arrays
Union of 2 sorted arrays
Arrays
Easy
Union of two arrays can be defined as the common and distinct elements in the two arrays.
Given two sorted arrays of size n and m respectively, find their union.


Example 1:

Input:
n = 5, arr1[] = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}
m = 3, arr2 [] = {1, 2, 3}
Output: 1 2 3 4 5
Explanation: Distinct elements including
both the arrays are: 1 2 3 4 5.


Example 2:

Input:
n = 5, arr1[] = {2, 2, 3, 4, 5}
m = 5, arr2[] = {1, 1, 2, 3, 4}
Output: 1 2 3 4 5
Explanation: Distinct elements including
both the arrays are: 1 2 3 4 5.
Understand the problem and develop a solution approach.

-> Take two pointer i and j where i is for arr1 and j is for arr2 and traverse
-> While travsersing 3 cases arises
    -> arr1[ i ] == arr2[ j ]
        Here we found a common element, so insert only one element in the union.
        Let’s insert arr[i] in union and whenever we insert element we increment pointer while pointer is not equal to the inserted element
    -> arr1[i]<arr2[j]
        Here insert arr[i]
    -> arr1[i]>arr2[j]
        Here insert arr2[j]
-> Now check if elements of any array is left to traverse then traverse that array
-> Take two pointer i and j where i is for arr1 and j is for arr2 and traverse
-> While travsersing 3 cases arises
    -> arr1[ i ] == arr2[ j ]
        Here we found a common element, so insert only one element in the union.
        Let’s insert arr[i] in union and whenever we insert element we increment pointer while pointer is not equal to the inserted element
    -> arr1[i]<arr2[j]
        Here insert arr[i]
    -> arr1[i]>arr2[j]
        Here insert arr2[j]
-> Now check if elements of any array is left to traverse then traverse that array
Time complexity: O(N+M)
Space complexity: O(0)
