  '[]', '{"format":"sections","sections":[{"id":"statement","title":"Problem Statement","kind":"problem-statement","bodyMd":"You are given an n x n 2D matrix representing an image, rotate the image by 90 degrees (clockwise).\n\nExample 1:\nInput: matrix = [[1,2,3],[4,5,6],[7,8,9]]\nOutput: [[7,4,1],[8,5,2],[9,6,3]]\n\nExample 2:\nInput: matrix = [[5,1,9,11],[2,4,8,10],[13,3,6,7],[15,14,12,16]]\nOutput: [[15,13,2,5],[14,3,4,1],[12,6,8,9],[16,7,10,11]]","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-intuition","title":"Brute Force Intuition","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Understand the problem and develop a solution approach.\n\nTo rotate the image by 90 degrees clockwise in-place, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Transpose the matrix: Iterate over the matrix and swap each element (i, j) with its corresponding element (j, i). This step transforms rows into columns.\n\n2. Reverse each row: Iterate over each row in the transposed matrix and reverse the elements. This step ensures the rotation in a clockwise direction.","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-approach","title":"Brute Force Approach","kind":"solution","bodyMd":"To rotate the image by 90 degrees clockwise in-place, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Transpose the matrix: Iterate over the matrix and swap each element (i, j) with its corresponding element (j, i). This step transforms rows into columns.\n\n2. Reverse each row: Iterate over each row in the transposed matrix and reverse the elements. This step ensures the rotation in a clockwise direction.","codeBlocks":[],"metadata":{"time":"O(N^2), where N is the size of the matrix.","space":"O(1)"},"visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-complexity","title":"Brute Force Complexity","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Time complexity: O(N^2), where N is the size of the matrix.\nSpace complexity: O(1)","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-quick-revision","title":"Brute Force Quick Revision","kind":"checklist","bodyMd":"- [ ] To rotate the image by 90 degrees clockwise in-place, we can follow these steps:\n- [ ] 1. Transpose the matrix: Iterate over the matrix and swap each element (i, j) with its corresponding element (j, i). This step transforms rows into columns.\n- [ ] 2. Reverse each row: Iterate over each row in the transposed matrix and reverse the elements. This step ensures the rotation in a clockwise direction."}]}', 
  '[]', '[]', '[]',
  'rotate-matrix
Rotate matrix
Arrays
Medium
You are given an n x n 2D matrix representing an image, rotate the image by 90 degrees (clockwise).

Example 1:
Input: matrix = [[1,2,3],[4,5,6],[7,8,9]]
Output: [[7,4,1],[8,5,2],[9,6,3]]

Example 2:
Input: matrix = [[5,1,9,11],[2,4,8,10],[13,3,6,7],[15,14,12,16]]
Output: [[15,13,2,5],[14,3,4,1],[12,6,8,9],[16,7,10,11]]
Understand the problem and develop a solution approach.

To rotate the image by 90 degrees clockwise in-place, we can follow these steps:

1. Transpose the matrix: Iterate over the matrix and swap each element (i, j) with its corresponding element (j, i). This step transforms rows into columns.

2. Reverse each row: Iterate over each row in the transposed matrix and reverse the elements. This step ensures the rotation in a clockwise direction.
To rotate the image by 90 degrees clockwise in-place, we can follow these steps:

1. Transpose the matrix: Iterate over the matrix and swap each element (i, j) with its corresponding element (j, i). This step transforms rows into columns.

2. Reverse each row: Iterate over each row in the transposed matrix and reverse the elements. This step ensures the rotation in a clockwise direction.
Time complexity: O(N^2), where N is the size of the matrix.
Space complexity: O(1)
