  '[]', '{"format":"sections","sections":[{"id":"statement","title":"Problem Statement","kind":"problem-statement","bodyMd":"Given an array of intervals intervals where intervals[i] = [start, end], return the minimum number of intervals you need to remove to make the rest of the intervals non-overlapping.","visuals":[]},{"id":"input-output","title":"Input / Output","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"### Input\n- intervals: [[start, end]]\n\n### Output\n- Return minimum number of intervals to remove","visuals":[]},{"id":"example","title":"Example","kind":"example","bodyMd":"```txt\nintervals = [[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[1,3]]\n```","visuals":[]},{"id":"example-explanation","title":"Example Explanation","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"We remove [1,3] to make the rest non-overlapping.\n\nRemaining:\n[[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]]\n\nAnswer = 1","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-intuition","title":"Brute Force Intuition","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Try removing each interval and check if the remaining intervals are non-overlapping. Track minimum removals.","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-approach","title":"Brute Force Approach","kind":"solution","bodyMd":"1. Generate subsets by removing intervals\n2. Check if remaining intervals are non-overlapping\n3. Track minimum removals","codeBlocks":[{"language":"java","title":"Brute Force Java","code":"// Brute force is exponential and not practical"}],"metadata":{"time":"O(2^N)","space":"O(N)"},"visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-complexity","title":"Brute Force Complexity","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"All subsets explored → exponential complexity.","visuals":[]},{"id":"optimal-intuition","title":"Optimal Intuition","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"To minimize removals, maximize number of non-overlapping intervals. Use greedy: always pick interval with smallest end time.","visuals":[]},{"id":"optimal-approach","title":"Optimal Approach","kind":"solution","bodyMd":"1. Sort by end time\n2. Traverse intervals\n3. If overlap → remove\n4. Else → update prevEnd","codeBlocks":[{"language":"java","title":"Optimal Java","code":"import java.util.*;\n\nclass Solution {\n    public int eraseOverlapIntervals(int[][] intervals) {\n        Arrays.sort(intervals, (a, b) -> a[1] - b[1]);\n\n        int count = 0;\n        int prevEnd = intervals[0][1];\n\n        for (int i = 1; i < intervals.length; i++) {\n            if (intervals[i][0] < prevEnd) {\n                count++;\n            } else {\n                prevEnd = intervals[i][1];\n            }\n        }\n\n        return count;\n    }\n}"}],"metadata":{"time":"O(N log N)","space":"O(1)"},"visuals":[]},{"id":"optimal-dry-run","title":"Optimal Dry Run","kind":"dry-run","bodyMd":"Sort → [[1,2],[1,3],[2,3],[3,4]]\n\nPick [1,2]\n[1,3] overlaps → remove\n[2,3] keep\n[3,4] keep\n\nAnswer = 1"},{"id":"optimal-complexity","title":"Optimal Complexity","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Sorting dominates → O(N log N).","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-quick-revision","title":"Brute Force Quick Revision","kind":"checklist","bodyMd":"- [ ] Try all removals\n- [ ] Check validity\n- [ ] Exponential"}]}', 
