  'rotting-oranges', 'problem', 'Rotting Oranges', '', 'revision-ready', 'public',
  'leetcode', 'https://leetcode.com/problems/rotting-oranges/', 'medium', 'Graph', 'Multi-source BFS',
  '[]', '{"format":"sections","sections":[{"id":"statement","title":"Problem Statement","kind":"problem-statement","bodyMd":"You are given an m x n grid where each cell can have one of three values:\n0 → empty cell\n1 → fresh orange\n2 → rotten orange\n\nEvery minute, any fresh orange adjacent (4-directionally) to a rotten orange becomes rotten.\n\nReturn the minimum number of minutes required to rot all oranges. If impossible, return -1.","visuals":[]},{"id":"input-output","title":"Input / Output","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"### Input\nA 2D grid of size m x n containing values 0, 1, or 2.\n\n### Output\nReturn minimum minutes required to rot all oranges, or -1 if not possible.","visuals":[]},{"id":"example","title":"Example","kind":"example","bodyMd":"Input:\ngrid = [[2,1,1],[1,1,0],[0,1,1]]\n\nOutput:\n4","visuals":[]},{"id":"example-explanation","title":"Example Explanation","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"All rotten oranges spread simultaneously. Each BFS level represents 1 minute.\n\nMinute 0: Initial rotten oranges\nMinute 1+: Spread to adjacent fresh oranges\n\nFinal answer = total BFS levels required","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-intuition","title":"Brute Force Intuition","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Simulate minute by minute. For each minute, scan the entire grid and convert fresh oranges adjacent to rotten ones. Repeat until no changes occur.","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-approach","title":"Brute Force Approach","kind":"solution","bodyMd":"1. Loop until no changes occur\n2. Traverse full grid\n3. For each rotten orange, mark adjacent fresh oranges\n4. Apply updates\n5. Count minutes","codeBlocks":[{"language":"java","title":"Brute Force Java","code":"class Solution {\n    public int orangesRotting(int[][] grid) {\n        int m = grid.length, n = grid[0].length;\n        int minutes = 0;\n        boolean changed;\n\n        do {\n            changed = false;\n            int[][] copy = new int[m][n];\n\n            for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n                for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n                    copy[i][j] = grid[i][j];\n                }\n            }\n\n            for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n                for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n                    if (grid[i][j] == 2) {\n                        int[][] dir = {{1,0},{-1,0},{0,1},{0,-1}};\n                        for (int[] d : dir) {\n                            int ni = i + d[0], nj = j + d[1];\n                            if (ni>=0 && nj>=0 && ni<m && nj<n && grid[ni][nj] == 1) {\n                                copy[ni][nj] = 2;\n                                changed = true;\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            if (changed) minutes++;\n            grid = copy;\n\n        } while (changed);\n\n        for (int[] row : grid) {\n            for (int cell : row) {\n                if (cell == 1) return -1;\n            }\n        }\n\n        return minutes;\n    }\n}"}],"metadata":{"time":"O((m*n)^2)","space":"O(m*n)"},"visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-complexity","title":"Brute Force Complexity","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Each iteration scans full grid, and worst-case we do this O(m*n) times.","visuals":[]},{"id":"optimal-intuition","title":"Optimal Intuition","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"All rotten oranges act as starting points. Spread happens simultaneously → BFS level order traversal.","visuals":[]},{"id":"optimal-approach","title":"Optimal Approach","kind":"solution","bodyMd":"1. Add all rotten oranges to queue\n2. Count fresh oranges\n3. Perform BFS\n4. For each level:\n   - Rot adjacent fresh oranges\n   - Decrease fresh count\n5. Increment time per level\n6. If fresh remains → return -1","codeBlocks":[{"language":"java","title":"Optimal Java","code":"class Solution {\n    public int orangesRotting(int[][] grid) {\n        int m = grid.length, n = grid[0].length;\n        Queue<int[]> q = new LinkedList<>();\n        int fresh = 0;\n\n      \t// push all rotten ones in the queue and counting fresh ones\n        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n                if (grid[i][j] == 2) q.offer(new int[]{i, j});\n                if (grid[i][j] == 1) fresh++;\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (fresh == 0) return 0;\n\n        int time = 0;\n        int[][] dir = {{1,0},{-1,0},{0,1},{0,-1}}; // this is just for going to four direction like [i-1,j],[i,j-1] ...\n\n        while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n            int size = q.size();\n            boolean spread = false;\n\n          \t// iterate till total level\n            for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n                int[] curr = q.poll();\n\n                // iterate over all four neighbours\n                for (int[] d : dir) {\n                    int ni = curr[0] + d[0];\n                    int nj = curr[1] + d[1];\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n                  \t// if fresh and not visited and exist then add to queue and make it rotten\n                    if (ni>=0 && nj>=0 && ni<m && nj<n && grid[ni][nj] == 1) {\n                        grid[ni][nj] = 2; // making 2 so that again we do not have to visit this one as we have condition for one\n                        q.offer(new int[]{ni, nj});\n                        fresh--;\n                        spread = true;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            if (spread) time++; // how many time it spread\n        }\n\n        return fresh == 0 ? time : -1;\n    }\n}\n"}],"metadata":{"time":"O(m*n)","space":"O(m*n)"},"visuals":[]},{"id":"optimal-dry-run","title":"Optimal Dry Run","kind":"dry-run","bodyMd":"Queue initially has all rotten oranges.\nEach BFS level spreads rot.\nTime increments after each level."},{"id":"optimal-complexity","title":"Optimal Complexity","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Each cell is processed once in BFS.","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-quick-revision","title":"Brute Force Quick Revision","kind":"checklist","bodyMd":"- [ ] Simulate minute-by-minute\n- [ ] Scan full grid repeatedly\n- [ ] High time complexity"}]}', 
  '["Multi-source BFS","Each level = 1 minute","Process all rotten together"]', '[]', '[]',
  'rotting-oranges
Rotting Oranges
Graph
Multi-source BFS
You are given an m x n grid where each cell can have one of three values:
0 → empty cell
1 → fresh orange
2 → rotten orange

Every minute, any fresh orange adjacent (4-directionally) to a rotten orange becomes rotten.

Return the minimum number of minutes required to rot all oranges. If impossible, return -1.
A 2D grid of size m x n containing values 0, 1, or 2.
Return minimum minutes required to rot all oranges, or -1 if not possible.
Input:
grid = [[2,1,1],[1,1,0],[0,1,1]]

Output:
4
All rotten oranges spread simultaneously. Each BFS level represents 1 minute.

Minute 0: Initial rotten oranges
Minute 1+: Spread to adjacent fresh oranges

Final answer = total BFS levels required
Simulate minute by minute. For each minute, scan the entire grid and convert fresh oranges adjacent to rotten ones. Repeat until no changes occur.
1. Loop until no changes occur
2. Traverse full grid
3. For each rotten orange, mark adjacent fresh oranges
4. Apply updates
5. Count minutes
Each iteration processes entire grid → inefficient.
Time increases even if few oranges are changing.
Each iteration scans full grid, and worst-case we do this O(m*n) times.
All rotten oranges act as starting points. Spread happens simultaneously → BFS level order traversal.
1. Add all rotten oranges to queue
2. Count fresh oranges
3. Perform BFS
4. For each level:
   - Rot adjacent fresh oranges
   - Decrease fresh count
5. Increment time per level
6. If fresh remains → return -1
Queue initially has all rotten oranges.
Each BFS level spreads rot.
Time increments after each level.
Each cell is processed once in BFS.
Simulate minute-by-minute
Scan full grid repeatedly
High time complexity
Multi-source BFS
Each level = 1 minute
Process all rotten together', '2026-04-12T14:35:08.119Z'
);

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_items (
  slug, type, title, summary, status, visibility,
  source, source_url, difficulty, topic, pattern,
