  'reorder-routes-to-make-all-paths-lead-to-zero', 'problem', 'Reorder Routes to Make All Paths Lead to the City Zero', '', 'revision-ready', 'public',
  'leetcode', 'https://leetcode.com/problems/reorder-routes-to-make-all-paths-lead-to-the-city-zero/', 'medium', 'Graph', 'DFS + Direction Tracking',
  '[]', '{"format":"sections","sections":[{"id":"statement","title":"Problem Statement","kind":"problem-statement","bodyMd":"There are n cities numbered from 0 to n-1 and n-1 roads such that there is exactly one path between any two cities.\n\nEach road is directed. You need to reorder some roads so that every city can reach city 0.\n\nReturn the minimum number of edges that need to be reversed.","visuals":[]},{"id":"input-output","title":"Input / Output","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"### Input\nn = number of cities\nconnections = list of directed edges [a, b] meaning a → b\n\n### Output\nReturn minimum number of edges to reverse so all nodes can reach city 0.","visuals":[]},{"id":"example","title":"Example","kind":"example","bodyMd":"Input:\nn = 6\nconnections = [[0,1],[1,3],[2,3],[4,0],[4,5]]\n\nOutput:\n3","visuals":[]},{"id":"example-explanation","title":"Example Explanation","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"We start DFS from node 0.\n\nIf an edge goes away from 0 (wrong direction), we need to reverse it.\nIf it already points towards 0, no change needed.","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-intuition","title":"Brute Force Intuition","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Try reversing different combinations of edges and check if all nodes can reach 0. This is inefficient due to exponential possibilities.","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-approach","title":"Brute Force Approach","kind":"solution","bodyMd":"1. Generate all combinations of edge reversals\n2. For each configuration:\n   - Check if all nodes can reach 0\n3. Return minimum reversals","codeBlocks":[{"language":"java","title":"Brute Force Java","code":"// Not practical brute force"}],"metadata":{"time":"O(2^E)","space":"O(E)"},"visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-complexity","title":"Brute Force Complexity","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Each edge can be reversed or not → exponential possibilities.","visuals":[]},{"id":"optimal-intuition","title":"Optimal Intuition","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Treat graph as undirected for traversal, but track original directions.\n\nWhile doing DFS from node 0:\n- If edge is in forward direction (away from 0), increment count\n- If edge is backward (towards 0), no action needed","visuals":[]},{"id":"optimal-approach","title":"Optimal Approach","kind":"solution","bodyMd":"1. Build two adjacency lists:\n   - forwardEdges (original direction)\n   - backwardEdges (reverse direction)\n2. Start DFS from node 0\n3. For each forward edge → increment answer\n4. For backward edges → just traverse\n5. Use visited array to avoid cycles","codeBlocks":[{"language":"java","title":"Optimal Java","code":"import java.util.*;\n\nclass Solution {\n    int ans = 0;\n\n    private void dfs(int node, boolean[] visited, List<Integer>[] forwardEdges, List<Integer>[] backwardEdges) {\n        visited[node] = true;\n\n        for (int ngh : forwardEdges[node]) {\n            if (!visited[ngh]) {\n                ans++; // wrong direction\n                dfs(ngh, visited, forwardEdges, backwardEdges);\n            }\n        }\n\n        for (int ngh : backwardEdges[node]) {\n            if (!visited[ngh]) {\n                dfs(ngh, visited, forwardEdges, backwardEdges);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    public int minReorder(int n, int[][] connections) {\n        boolean[] visited = new boolean[n];\n\n        List<Integer>[] forwardEdges = new ArrayList[n];\n        List<Integer>[] backwardEdges = new ArrayList[n];\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            forwardEdges[i] = new ArrayList<>();\n            backwardEdges[i] = new ArrayList<>();\n        }\n\n        for (int[] edge : connections) {\n            int a = edge[0], b = edge[1];\n            forwardEdges[a].add(b);\n            backwardEdges[b].add(a);\n        }\n\n        dfs(0, visited, forwardEdges, backwardEdges);\n        return ans;\n    }\n}"}],"metadata":{"time":"O(n)","space":"O(n)"},"visuals":[]},{"id":"optimal-dry-run","title":"Optimal Dry Run","kind":"dry-run","bodyMd":"Start from 0 → go to neighbors\nIf edge direction is away → ans++\nContinue DFS until all nodes visited"},{"id":"optimal-complexity","title":"Optimal Complexity","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Each node and edge is visited once during DFS.","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-quick-revision","title":"Brute Force Quick Revision","kind":"checklist","bodyMd":"- [ ] Try all edge reversals\n- [ ] Check reachability\n- [ ] Exponential time"}]}', 
  '["DFS from node 0","Count forward edges","Ignore backward edges"]', '[]', '[]',
  'reorder-routes-to-make-all-paths-lead-to-zero
