  'max-consecutive-ones', 'problem', 'Max Consecutive Ones', '', 'revision-ready', 'public',
  'leetcode', 'https://leetcode.com/problems/max-consecutive-ones/', 'medium', 'Array', 'Linear Scan / Sliding Window',
  '[]', '{"format":"sections","sections":[{"id":"statement","title":"Problem Statement","kind":"problem-statement","bodyMd":"Given a binary array `nums`, return the maximum number of consecutive `1`s in the array.","visuals":[]},{"id":"input-output","title":"Input / Output","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"### Input\nA binary array `nums` consisting only of 0s and 1s.\n\n### Output\nAn integer representing the maximum count of consecutive 1s.","visuals":[]},{"id":"example","title":"Example","kind":"example","bodyMd":"Input: nums = [1,1,0,1,1,1]\nOutput: 3\nExplanation: The first two digits are consecutive 1s. The last three digits are consecutive 1s. The maximum number of consecutive 1s is 3.","visuals":[]},{"id":"example-explanation","title":"Example Explanation","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"We track the current streak of 1s. When we see a 1, we increment. When we see a 0, we check if the current streak was the longest we''ve seen so far, then reset to zero.","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-intuition","title":"Brute Force Intuition","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Check every possible subarray. If a subarray contains only 1s, calculate its length and keep track of the maximum length found.","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-approach","title":"Brute Force Approach","kind":"solution","bodyMd":"1. Use nested loops to generate all possible subarrays.\n2. For each subarray, check if every element is 1.\n3. If it is, update the maximum length.","codeBlocks":[{"language":"java","title":"Brute Force Java","code":"class Solution {\n    public int findMaxConsecutiveOnes(int[] nums) {\n        int max = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {\n            for (int j = i; j < nums.length; j++) {\n                boolean allOnes = true;\n                for (int k = i; k <= j; k++) {\n                    if (nums[k] != 1) {\n                        allOnes = false;\n                        break;\n                    }\n                }\n                if (allOnes) max = Math.max(max, j - i + 1);\n            }\n        }\n        return max;\n    }\n}"}],"metadata":{"time":"O(N^3)","space":"O(1)"},"visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-complexity","title":"Brute Force Complexity","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"Generating all subarrays is O(N^2), and checking each one is O(N).","visuals":[]},{"id":"optimal-intuition","title":"Optimal Intuition","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"As we walk through the array, we only need to know two things: ''What is my current streak?'' and ''What is the longest streak I have seen so far?''. We don''t need to look back at previous elements.","visuals":[]},{"id":"optimal-approach","title":"Optimal Approach","kind":"solution","bodyMd":"1. Initialize `count = 0` and `max = 0`.\n2. Iterate through each number in the array.\n3. If the number is 1, increment `count`.\n4. Update `max` using `Math.max(max, count)`.\n5. If the number is 0, reset `count` to 0.\n6. Return `max`.","codeBlocks":[{"language":"java","title":"Optimal Java","code":"class Solution {\n    public int findMaxConsecutiveOnes(int[] nums) {\n        int max = 0;\n        int currentCount = 0;\n        for (int num : nums) {\n            if (num == 1) {\n                currentCount++;\n                if (currentCount > max) max = currentCount;\n            } else {\n                currentCount = 0;\n            }\n        }\n        return max;\n    }\n}"}],"metadata":{"time":"O(N)","space":"O(1)"},"visuals":[]},{"id":"optimal-dry-run","title":"Optimal Dry Run","kind":"dry-run","bodyMd":"nums = [1,1,0,1]\n- i=0: count=1, max=1\n- i=1: count=2, max=2\n- i=2: count=0, max=2\n- i=3: count=1, max=2\nResult: 2"},{"id":"optimal-complexity","title":"Optimal Complexity","kind":"markdown","bodyMd":"We traverse the array once, performing constant time operations at each step.","visuals":[]},{"id":"brute-quick-revision","title":"Brute Force Quick Revision","kind":"checklist","bodyMd":"- [ ] Check every subarray\n- [ ] O(N^3) or O(N^2) time"}]}', 
  '["Linear Scan","Maintain current streak counter","Reset counter when element is 0","Keep global maximum","O(N) time"]', '[]', '[]',
  'max-consecutive-ones
Max Consecutive Ones
Array
Linear Scan / Sliding Window
Given a binary array `nums`, return the maximum number of consecutive `1`s in the array.
A binary array `nums` consisting only of 0s and 1s.
An integer representing the maximum count of consecutive 1s.
Input: nums = [1,1,0,1,1,1]
Output: 3
Explanation: The first two digits are consecutive 1s. The last three digits are consecutive 1s. The maximum number of consecutive 1s is 3.
We track the current streak of 1s. When we see a 1, we increment. When we see a 0, we check if the current streak was the longest we''ve seen so far, then reset to zero.
Check every possible subarray. If a subarray contains only 1s, calculate its length and keep track of the maximum length found.
1. Use nested loops to generate all possible subarrays.
2. For each subarray, check if every element is 1.
3. If it is, update the maximum length.
nums = [1,0,1,1]
Subarrays of 1s: [1], [1], [1,1]
Max length: 2
Generating all subarrays is O(N^2), and checking each one is O(N).
As we walk through the array, we only need to know two things: ''What is my current streak?'' and ''What is the longest streak I have seen so far?''. We don''t need to look back at previous elements.
1. Initialize `count = 0` and `max = 0`.
2. Iterate through each number in the array.
3. If the number is 1, increment `count`.
4. Update `max` using `Math.max(max, count)`.
5. If the number is 0, reset `count` to 0.
6. Return `max`.
nums = [1,1,0,1]
- i=0: count=1, max=1
- i=1: count=2, max=2
- i=2: count=0, max=2
- i=3: count=1, max=2
Result: 2
We traverse the array once, performing constant time operations at each step.
Check every subarray
O(N^3) or O(N^2) time
Linear Scan
Maintain current streak counter
Reset counter when element is 0
Keep global maximum
O(N) time', '2026-04-15T06:51:58.852Z'
);

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_items (
  slug, type, title, summary, status, visibility,
